{
  "_README": [
    "Hand-curated section -> concept mappings, keyed by section_id.",
    "Each value is a list of [concept_id, relevance] pairs.",
    "",
    "This is the INVERSE of concept_map.json's maps_to, and it is authored this",
    "way on purpose: it was derived by walking the section titles act by act, so",
    "the reviewable question is 'is this section tagged correctly?' rather than",
    "'did we forget a section?'. tools/build_concept_map.py inverts it and merges",
    "it into data/ontology/concept_map.json, preserving the existing",
    "descriptions/aliases and the mappings that were already there.",
    "",
    "relevance: 'primary'    = this section directly governs the concept",
    "           'supporting' = relevant context, not the operative rule",
    "",
    "Sections deliberately omitted are pure machinery (power to make rules,",
    "delegation of powers, protection of action taken in good faith) or PDF",
    "parsing artifacts (IDA 3/4/5, KSEA 23), which carry no user-answerable rule.",
    "MWA_1948 is repealed by COW_2019 s.69; its existing mappings are left in",
    "place as a historical record but retrieval suppresses them."
  ],

  "extra_aliases": {
    "_note": [
      "Additional natural phrasings merged onto EXISTING concepts by the",
      "builder. Kept here rather than edited straight into concept_map.json so",
      "every ontology change this project makes is reproducible from tools/.",
      "Each of these is a phrasing a real user typed (or would plausibly type)",
      "that the original alias list missed. Grounding is substring-first, so an",
      "alias only helps if it appears verbatim inside the query — prefer short,",
      "natural fragments over full sentences."
    ],
